Third-party software and sources
--------------------------------

Version 0.1 is a map of analysis pathways and runs no analyses. The map
describes, and later releases will call, the following R packages. Each is
distributed under its own license; cite them as their authors ask, by running
citation("<package>") in R.

  metafor     https://cran.r-project.org/package=metafor
              Viechtbauer W (2010). Conducting meta-analyses in R with the
              metafor package. Journal of Statistical Software, 36(3), 1-48.
  meta        https://cran.r-project.org/package=meta
  netmeta     https://cran.r-project.org/package=netmeta
  gemtc       https://cran.r-project.org/package=gemtc
  multinma    https://cran.r-project.org/package=multinma
  bayesmeta   https://cran.r-project.org/package=bayesmeta
  lme4        https://cran.r-project.org/package=lme4
  dtametaTMB  https://cran.r-project.org/package=dtametaTMB
  metamisc    https://cran.r-project.org/package=metamisc
  dosresmeta  https://cran.r-project.org/package=dosresmeta

The R service (r_service/) also uses these R packages, pinned in
r_service/renv.lock:

  plumber     https://cran.r-project.org/package=plumber
  jsonlite    https://cran.r-project.org/package=jsonlite
  metadat     https://cran.r-project.org/package=metadat (the datasets its tests use)

The backend (backend/) uses these Python packages, pinned in
backend/requirements.txt with the packages they depend on. Those are under
MIT, BSD-3-Clause or Apache-2.0, except certifi (MPL-2.0) and
typing_extensions (PSF-2.0); all are compatible with the GPL:

  FastAPI     https://fastapi.tiangolo.com (MIT)
  Pydantic    https://docs.pydantic.dev (MIT)
  Uvicorn     https://www.uvicorn.org (BSD-3-Clause)
  HTTPX       https://www.python-httpx.org (BSD-3-Clause)

The methodological content of the map cites the Cochrane Handbook for
Systematic Reviews of Interventions (https://www.cochrane.org/authors/handbooks-and-manuals/handbook),
the Cochrane Handbook for Systematic Reviews of Diagnostic Test Accuracy,
methods papers, and the documentation of the packages above. Every source used is listed, with
its link, in spec/backbone.md.

The web app bundles these JavaScript packages, each under the MIT license,
with the dependencies they bring (MIT or BSD-3-Clause):

  React, React DOM   https://react.dev
  React Router       https://reactrouter.com
  three.js           https://threejs.org
  react-three-fiber  https://github.com/pmndrs/react-three-fiber

Every npm package the app uses or is built with, with its version and
licence, is listed in docs/npm-licences.md, which is generated from
frontend/package-lock.json.

Fonts used by the map page (IBM Plex) are loaded from Google Fonts and are
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
